#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:1
msgid "Threat Model for qs (querystring parsing library)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:3
msgid "1. Library Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:5
msgid "**Library Name:** qs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:6
msgid ""
"**Brief Description:** A JavaScript library for parsing and stringifying "
"URL query strings, supporting nested objects and arrays. It is widely "
"used in Node.js and web applications for processing query "
"parameters[2][6][8]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:7
msgid "**Key Public APIs/Functions:** `qs.parse()`, `qs.stringify()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:9
msgid "2. Define Scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:11
msgid ""
"This threat model focuses on the core parsing and stringifying "
"functionality, specifically the handling of nested objects and arrays, "
"option validation, and cycle management in stringification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:13
msgid "3. Conceptual System Diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:26
msgid "**Trust Boundaries:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:27
msgid ""
"**Input string (parse):** May come from untrusted sources (e.g., user "
"input, network requests)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:28
msgid ""
"**Input object (stringify):** May contain cycles, which can lead to "
"infinite loops during stringification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:29
msgid "**Options:** Provided by the caller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:30
msgid ""
"**Cycle Tracking:** Used only during stringification to detect and handle"
" circular references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:32
msgid "4. Identify Assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:34
msgid ""
"**Integrity of parsed output:** Prevent malicious manipulation of the "
"output object structure, especially ensuring builtins/globals are not "
"modified as a result of parse[3][4][8]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:35
msgid ""
"**Confidentiality of processed data:** Avoid leaking sensitive "
"information through errors or output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:36
msgid ""
"**Availability/performance for host application:** Prevent crashes or "
"resource exhaustion in the consuming application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:37
msgid ""
"**Security of host application:** Prevent the library from being a vector"
" for attacks (e.g., prototype pollution, DoS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:38
msgid ""
"**Reputation of library:** Maintain trust by avoiding supply chain "
"attacks and vulnerabilities[1]."
msgstr ""

