#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:49
msgid "**Key Threats:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:50
msgid ""
"**Tampering:** Malicious input can, if not prevented, alter parsed output"
" (e.g., prototype pollution via `__proto__`, modification of "
"builtins/globals)[3][4][8]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:51
msgid ""
"**Information Disclosure:** Error messages may expose internal details or"
" sensitive data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:52
msgid "**Denial of Service:** Large or malformed input can exhaust memory or CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:53
msgid ""
"**Elevation of Privilege:** Prototype pollution can lead to unintended "
"privilege escalation in the host application[3][4][8]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:55
msgid "6. Mitigation/Countermeasures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid "Threat Identified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid "Proposed Mitigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid "Tampering (malicious input, prototype pollution)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid ""
"Strict input validation; keep `allowPrototypes: false` by default; use "
"`plainObjects` for output; ensure builtins/globals are never modified by "
"parse[4][8]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid "Information Disclosure (error messages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid "Generic error messages without stack traces or internal paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid "Denial of Service (memory/CPU exhaustion)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid ""
"Enforce `arrayLimit` and `parameterLimit` with safe defaults; enable "
"`throwOnLimitExceeded`; limit nesting depth[7]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid "Elevation of Privilege (prototype pollution)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md
msgid ""
"Keep `allowPrototypes: false`; validate options against allowlist; use "
"`plainObjects` to avoid prototype pollution[4][8]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:64
msgid "7. Risk Ranking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:66
msgid ""
"**High:** Denial of Service via array parsing or malformed input "
"(historical vulnerability)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:67
msgid ""
"**Medium:** Prototype pollution via options or input (if "
"`allowPrototypes` enabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:68
msgid "**Low:** Information disclosure in errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:70
msgid "8. Next Steps & Review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:72
msgid "**Audit option validation logic.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:73
msgid "**Add depth limiting to nested parsing and stringification.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:74
msgid "**Implement fuzz testing for parser and stringifier edge cases.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:75
msgid "**Regularly review dependencies for vulnerabilities.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:76
msgid "**Keep documentation and threat model up to date.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:77
msgid "**Ensure builtins/globals are never modified as a result of parse.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/.github_THREAT_MODEL.md:78
msgid ""
"**Support round-trip consistency between parse and stringify as a non-"
"security goal, with the right options[5][9].**"
msgstr ""

